# Marriott International Corporate Brand Standards

You are working in a Marriott International corporate presentation context. Apply these standards in every interaction.

## Color Palette

| Token | Hex | Use |
|---|---|---|
| Marriott Red | `#BE202E` | Title slides, section dividers, key stats, accent lines |
| Marriott Dark | `#1D1D1B` | Body text, dark backgrounds |
| Corporate Gray | `#4A4A4A` | Secondary text, subheadings |
| Light Gray | `#F2F2F2` | Slide backgrounds, card fills |
| Mid Gray | `#9B9B9B` | Captions, footnotes, muted text |
| White | `#FFFFFF` | Backgrounds, reverse text |
| Gold (use sparingly) | `#B8973A` | Luxury emphasis only, thin dividers |

**Color rules:**
- Red is accent — never fill large areas with red except title and section slides
- Never use red text on a red background
- Body text is always Dark (`#1D1D1B`) on light backgrounds
- White text only on Dark or Red backgrounds

## Typography

**Font stack (internal corporate):** Arial, Calibri, Helvetica Neue, sans-serif

| Element | Size | Weight |
|---|---|---|
| Deck title | 44-52pt | Regular |
| Slide title | 26-32pt | Regular |
| Subtitle / eyebrow | 14-16pt | Regular |
| Body / bullets | 13-15pt | Regular |
| Caption / footnote | 10-11pt | Regular |

**Type rules:**
- Title case for slide titles
- Sentence case for body copy and bullets
- Never use decorative or display fonts
- Minimum body size: 12pt
- Do not use bold for entire paragraphs — bold only for emphasis within a sentence

## Slide Writing Rules

### One idea per slide
Every slide must have exactly one main idea. If you find yourself writing "and also..." on a slide, that is a second slide.

### Insight headlines, not topic labels
Slide titles must state the insight, not just the topic.
- ❌ "Q2 Results"
- ✓ "Q2 revenue exceeded forecast by 14%"
- ❌ "Cursor adoption"
- ✓ "Team Cursor usage grew 40% in 90 days with no formal rollout"

### Bullets
- Maximum 5 bullets per slide
- Maximum ~12 words per bullet (shorter is always better)
- No nested bullets — depth comes from the assertion + detail form instead
- Every bullet is a complete thought, not a label
- Start bullets with a verb when possible

### Assertion + detail (how bullets carry depth)
Prefer the two-line bullet form: a bold assertion (`text`) followed by one indented evidence line (`detail`) — the number, example, or name that proves the claim. This is the sanctioned way to add depth; it is not a nested bullet.
- ❌ "Improve deck quality"
- ✓ text: "Cut deck production from days to minutes" · detail: "Last 3 briefs exported in under 10 minutes each"

### Lead with the conclusion
The most important information goes first. Do not build to the conclusion — state it, then support it.

### Speaker notes are part of the slide
Every slide ships with a structured talk track in the PPTX notes pane: opening line, 2–4 points that go beyond the slide text, a transition, and a time estimate. A deck without speaker notes is not done.

## Brand Voice

**Tone:** Clear, confident, warm, action-oriented.

**Avoid:**
- "Going forward" → use "from here" or just state what happens
- "Leverage" → use "use"
- "Synergies" → describe the actual benefit
- "Best-in-class" → cite the evidence instead
- "In this space" → be specific
- Passive voice wherever possible

**Numbers:**
- Round to the meaningful digit (1,200 not 1,197)
- Always include context (1,200 engineers — up from 800 last year)
- Use % for comparisons, absolute numbers for scale

## Layout style

Selected layout: **Executive Classic** (`classic`) — Primary title slides, clear accent bars

Layout style is Executive Classic. Prefer primary/full-bleed title and section slides. Use content slides with a clear insight headline and short bullets. Metrics tiles on light gray. Keep visual density moderate — do not overcrowd.

**Slide mix hint:** Balanced mix: title, optional agenda, content, metrics, chart/diagram where the story is numeric or process, closing. Section dividers when the deck exceeds ~10 slides. Prefer diagram/chart over image.

The PPTX exporter (`bundled/export-pptx.cjs`) reads layout from `brand/brand-pack.json` (`layoutStyle`) or `DECK_LAYOUT`. Default dogfood layout is classic.

## Slide Type Reference

1. **Title** — Red or dark background, white text, deck title + subtitle
2. **Agenda** — Light background, numbered items, title in Red
3. **Section divider** — Red background, section number and title
4. **Content (single)** — White background, insight headline, bullets or narrative
5. **Two-column** — White background, side-by-side comparison
6. **Metrics** — White or light gray background, 2-4 large stat blocks in Red
7. **Quote** — Light gray or red background, large pull quote, attribution
8. **Closing / Next steps** — Numbered action list, consistent with opening style
9. **Chart** — Native PPTX chart from JSON series (trends and comparisons)
10. **Diagram** — Process / architecture / swimlane from structured nodes (exporter draws shapes)
11. **Image** — Agent-generated illustration in `assets/` (prefer diagram/chart when possible)

## What Not to Do

- Do not use clip art, stock photo collages, or 3D effects
- Do not ask humans to drop PNGs into `assets/` — `visual-creator` generates image slides during `/build-deck`
- Do not invent precise chart numbers that are not in the brief
- Do not use more than 2 typefaces per slide
- Do not use WordArt or text shadows
- Do not include a slide title that is longer than one line
- Do not create slides that are purely decorative with no information
- Do not include your working notes or "draft" text in slides shared externally
